ings up try signing out of the app on the device that is accessing the Kids Profile, then sign back in.\nL57: \nL58: \nL59: Did this answer your question?\nL60: \nL61: 【3†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL62: \nL63: \nL64: \nL65: 【4†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL66: \nL67:  Back to top\nL68: \nL69: 【5†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL70: \nL71: 【6†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL72: ## Need more assistance?\nL73: \nL74: 【7†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL75: \nL76: \nL77: \nL78: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL79: \nL80: \nL81: \nL82: Worst\nL83: \nL84: 1\nL85: \nL86: 2\nL87: \nL88: 3\nL89: \nL90: 4\nL91: \nL92: 5\nL93: \nL94: 6\nL95: \nL96: 7\nL97: \nL98: Best\nL99: \nL100: \nL101: \nL102: Region\nL103: \nL104: United States\nL105: \nL106: Language\nL107: \nL108: English\nL109: \nL110: Loading\nL111: \nL112: Remove titles from Kids Profile 【8†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList is only partly shared (https://help.audible.com/s/article/collection-is-only-partly-shared)\nciteturn999view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view1\",\"id\":6}); Total lines: 83\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Kids Profile Profiles\nL13: ## List is only partly shared\nL14: \nL15:   * Jun 18, 2025\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: List is only partly shared\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: collection-is-only-partly-shared\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: If you're seeing a \"Partly shared\" status badge next to a list in your Library, it can mean that the Audible editors have added new titles to the list, in which case you'll need to update the list in your Library first and then re-share it to your Kids Profile.\nL29: \nL30: Did this answer your question?\nL31: \nL32: 【1†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL33: \nL34: \nL35: \nL36: 【2†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL37:  Back to top\nL38: \nL39: 【3†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL40: \nL41: 【4†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL42: ## Need more assistance?\nL43: \nL44: 【5†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL45: \nL46: \nL47: \nL48: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL49: \nL50: \nL51: \nL52: Worst\nL53: \nL54: 1\nL55: \nL56: 2\nL57: \nL58: 3\nL59: \nL60: 4\nL61: \nL62: 5\nL63: \nL64: 6\nL65: \nL66: 7\nL67: \nL68: Best\nL69: \nL70: \nL71: \nL72: Region\nL73: \nL74: United States\nL75: \nL76: Language\nL77: \nL78: English\nL79: \nL80: Loading\nL81: \nL82: List is only partly shared 【6†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nView Your Listening Stats (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-your-listening-stats)\nciteturn999view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":34}); Total lines: 106\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Listening Profiles\nL13: ## View Your Listening Stats\nL14: \nL15:   * May 13, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: View Your Listening Stats\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: view-your-listening-stats\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Listening stats is a feature that gives you deeper insights on your listening behavior, tracks your progress, and celebrates your listening milestones.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31: \nL32:   * 【1†Where can I see my listening stats?】\nL33:   * 【2†Who can access listening stats?】\nL34:   * 【3†How often are my listening stats updated?】\nL35:   * 【4†Can I share my listening stats with others? 】\nL36: ## Where can I see my listening stats?\nL37: \nL38:   1. Open the Audible app and sign in.\nL39:   2. Select Profile.\nL40:   3. Scroll to and select Listening stats.\nL41: \nL42: ## Who can access listening stats?\nL43: \nL44: Listening stats are available to all signed-in Audible customers. The personalized insights are tailored to your listening history and preferences.\nL45: ## How often are my listening stats updated?\nL46: \nL47: Listening stats are updated in real-time as you listen on Audible. Certain insights about your evolving listening journey, such as your top genres, are updated monthly.\nL48: ## Can I share my listening stats with others?\nL49: \nL50: Yes, you can share select listening stats and milestones with your friends, family, or on social networks via the Share my stats feature on the listening stats page.\nL51: \nL52: Did this answer your question?\nL53: \nL54: 【5†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL55: \nL56: \nL57: \nL58: 【6†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL59: \nL60:  Back to top\nL61: \nL62: 【7†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL63: \nL64: 【8†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL65: ## Need more assistance?\nL66: \nL67: 【9†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL68: \nL69: \nL70: \nL71: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL72: \nL73: \nL74: \nL75: Worst\nL76: \nL77: 1\nL78: \nL79: 2\nL80: \nL81: 3\nL82: \nL83: 4\nL84: \nL85: 5\nL86: \nL87: 6\nL88: \nL89: 7\nL90: \nL91: Best\nL92: \nL93: \nL94: \nL95: Region\nL96: \nL97: United States\nL98: \nL99: Language\nL100: \nL101: English\nL102: \nL103: Loading\nL104: \nL105: View Your Listening Stats 【10†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDiscover new audiobooks with Maven (https://help.audible.com/s/article/discover-new-audiobooks-with-maven)\nciteturn999view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":19}); Total lines: 135\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Getting started Library Listening Ways to listen\nL13: ## Discover new audiobooks with Maven\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Discover new audiobooks with Maven\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: discover-new-audiobooks-with-maven\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Maven is an AI-powered content discovery feature that helps you find your next listen. Chat with Maven to receive tailored audiobook recommendations, easily compare potential titles, and get a quick overview for any title in the catalog. Refine your results with follow-up questions to easily find and decide on your next listen.\nL29: Note: Maven is a built-in feature that's always accessible, but using it is entirely optional.\nL30: \nL31: In this article:\nL32: \nL33:   * 【1†How do I use Maven?】\nL34:   * 【2†What can I ask Maven?】\nL35: ## How do I use Maven?\nL36: \nL37: You can get tailored audiobook recommendations from Maven by following these steps:\nL38: \nL39: In the app\nL40:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL41:   2. Select the Search option.\nL42:   3. Select Ask Maven.\nL43:   4. Start a conversation by asking for title recommendations in your own words (e.g., \"Recommend a new thriller\" or \"What are some good sci-fi listens?\").\nL44:   5. Continue the chat to narrow down results, get more details, or compare titles:\nL45:      * Ask follow-up questions to refine suggestions.\nL46:      * Request a brief overview or more information on a recommended book.\nL47:      * Compare two titles to help you decide.\nL48: Note: You can return and resume your chat session within 24 hours.\nL49: \nL50: On desktop\nL51:   1. Select Find your next great listen.\nL52:   2. Select the Ask Maven icon to open the chat.\nL53:   3. Start a conversation by asking for title recommendations in your own words (e.g., \"Recommend a new thriller\" or \"What are some good sci-fi listens?\").\nL54:   4. Continue the chat to narrow down results, get more details, or compare titles:\nL55:      * Ask follow-up questions to refine suggestions.\nL56:      * Request a brief overview or more information on a recommended book.\nL57:      * Compare two titles to help you decide.\nL58: Note: You can return and resume your chat session within 24 hours.\nL59: \nL60: On mobile web\nL61:   1. Select Find your next great listen.\nL62:   2. Select the Ask Maven icon to open the chat.\nL63:   3. Start a conversation by asking for title recommendations in your own words (e.g., \"Recommend a new thriller\" or \"What are some good sci-fi listens?\").\nL64:   4. Continue the chat to narrow down results, get more details, or compare titles:\nL65:      * Ask follow-up questions to refine suggestions.\nL66:      * Request a brief overview or more information on a recommended book.\nL67:      * Compare two titles to help you decide.\nL68: Note: You can return and resume your chat session within 24 hours.\nL69: ## What can I ask Maven?\nL70: \nL71: Maven currently provides recommendations solely for audiobook titles and Audible Originals audiobooks, along with a brief overview to help you quickly decide on a listen. Here are some of the ways you can use Maven:\nL72:   * Finding something new: Random recommendations, or titles similar to books you've already loved.\nL73:   * Story details: Books featuring specific character identities, archetypes, and relationship dynamics.\nL74:   * Genre-specific: Filtered recommendations by genre, niche subgenres, and recurring themes.\nL75:   * Personal fit: Content that's included with your plan, or audiobooks tailored to specific interests.\nL76:   * Format preferences: Titles based on how they're performed (e.g., full cast, duet narration, narrator style) or a specific listening length.\nL77:   * Making a decision: Getting quick information on a recommendation, or comparing two titles side-by-side to choose the best one for you.\nL78:   * Featured content: Books recognized in celebrity book clubs, bestseller lists, award winners, Audible charts, and recent releases.\nL79: Note: Maven does not currently offer recommendations for podcasts or authors, nor does it provide in-depth audiobook details beyond the general overview. Maven is designed specifically for recommendations and cannot offer any form of account-related or technical support.\nL80: \nL81: Did this answer your question?\nL82: \nL83: 【3†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL84: \nL85: \nL86: \nL87: 【4†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL88: \nL89:  Back to top\nL90: \nL91: 【5†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL92: \nL93: 【6†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL94: ## Need more assistance?\nL95: \nL96: 【7†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL97: \nL98: \nL99: \nL100: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL101: \nL102: \nL103: \nL104: Worst\nL105: \nL106: 1\nL107: \nL108: 2\nL109: \nL110: 3\nL111: \nL112: 4\nL113: \nL114: 5\nL115: \nL116: 6\nL117: \nL118: 7\nL119: \nL120: Best\nL121: \nL122: \nL123: \nL124: Region\nL125: \nL126: United States\nL127: \nL128: Language\nL129: \nL130: English\nL131: \nL132: Loading\nL133: \nL134: Discover new audiobooks with Maven 【8†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
